                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1e1acbab-e514-42cb-962f-310f0a3662a6",
                        "entry_id": "a4a61c01-2c54-3a2d-97f3-e84ca1c22af0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more reversionist"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8f44f981-30aa-4c79-8a0a-0357ee4efd68",
                        "entry_id": "a4a61c01-2c54-3a2d-97f3-e84ca1c22af0",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most reversionist"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10340136-ee87-3d0b-b608-d8364eb99c86",
                        "entry_id": "a4a61c01-2c54-3a2d-97f3-e84ca1c22af0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to or characteristic of reversionists."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab5bb916-5d29-4381-87b4-4bf0a5080b66",
                                "sense_id": "10340136-ee87-3d0b-b608-d8364eb99c86",
                                "text": "Certain fringe ecologists are quite as reversionist in their thinking, and reach even farther back for their image of the good life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc64236e-58a8-447e-aab2-84f16e10abc6",
                                "sense_id": "10340136-ee87-3d0b-b608-d8364eb99c86",
                                "text": "This confirms that the design process is more reversionist than might be imagined."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82b7c6ef-1dca-4b78-9b52-591cc133fe3f",
                                "sense_id": "10340136-ee87-3d0b-b608-d8364eb99c86",
                                "text": "Second, the movement sheds light on the nature of 'reversionist thought supported by the Japan Reversionist Movement' (NakanoandArasaki 1976:85)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "33a219bd-5c7a-3fae-84b4-172b18fbd50c",
                "word": "reversionist",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b369fbbb-b90f-4969-9995-e8d692a66294",
                        "entry_id": "33a219bd-5c7a-3fae-84b4-172b18fbd50c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "reversionists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd5c0333-4efd-35b1-a823-64e3786103de",
                        "entry_id": "33a219bd-5c7a-3fae-84b4-172b18fbd50c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who clings to previous patterns of behavior or thought, rejecting social or cultural change."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb443b58-bd54-4704-82a8-c4ed8605a7dd",
                                "sense_id": "fd5c0333-4efd-35b1-a823-64e3786103de",
                                "text": "The right-wing Reversionist focuses on a small town past where law, order and predictability prevail."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9150409b-aa6e-444a-96fc-9c2e14042fa6",
                                "sense_id": "fd5c0333-4efd-35b1-a823-64e3786103de",
                                "text": "These reversionists think technology and industrialism are synonymous. They can't imagine clean technology, human technology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8af5077e-01c3-4ddb-b908-6719e47b5d0e",
                                "sense_id": "fd5c0333-4efd-35b1-a823-64e3786103de",
                                "text": "Far from being reversionists, Mateelians are constantly in search of non-polluting, low-energy technology to combine with their labor-intensive strategies and high-quality crafts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26e4c867-b51b-434b-968b-7386edb47b41",
                                "sense_id": "fd5c0333-4efd-35b1-a823-64e3786103de",
                                "text": "A dedicated reversionist, she considered Arthur to have been the last British monarch worthy of the crown. She would have re-instituted the maypole and the setting out of bowls of cream for goblins — despite lack of response to a saucer of Carnation Milk she three times thrice had left on the elegant proch of 3 Mather Gardens."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8dce1d41-0f4c-3b79-919d-151f829bf727",
                        "entry_id": "33a219bd-5c7a-3fae-84b4-172b18fbd50c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who has lost faith; a heathen, nonbeliever, or apostate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f2bb032-af34-4335-9752-840f3884d2e2",
                                "sense_id": "8dce1d41-0f4c-3b79-919d-151f829bf727",
                                "text": "But for the reversionist the indwelling of Christ has no effect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "246197f5-1522-45d3-9122-2ae0a0984f6b",
                                "sense_id": "8dce1d41-0f4c-3b79-919d-151f829bf727",
                                "text": "The reality which is expected is the justice of God judging unbeliever reversionists, both Jews and Gentiles, and sending them to the Lake of Fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d354e45-186b-4692-a79d-135cd613f33b",
                                "sense_id": "8dce1d41-0f4c-3b79-919d-151f829bf727",
                                "text": "Lot is a believer who is a monetary reversionist. He abandoned the directive will of God for \"sordid gain\" (cf. 1Tim. 3:8; Titus 1:7, 11; 1Pet. 5:2; Gk. aischrokerdes)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec17fd19-6a04-332c-873b-dee51e5ed707",
                        "entry_id": "33a219bd-5c7a-3fae-84b4-172b18fbd50c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The person to whom a property reverts when a freehold expires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "965918ab-779a-4424-a0f5-a90fdc83c4e3",
                                "sense_id": "ec17fd19-6a04-332c-873b-dee51e5ed707",
                                "text": "As to the argument about the possibility of the reversionist not being capable of discharging his duties, that would equally apply to the granting a place for one life, as then the holder might live so long, or become so infirm as to be unable to fulfil all the duties of his situation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17a05f02-a036-4360-857c-1bd6ff46de47",
                                "sense_id": "ec17fd19-6a04-332c-873b-dee51e5ed707",
                                "text": "If the particular species of clamour, to which we allude, has in some degree subsided, we doubt whether the cessateion of hostilities is so much to be ascribed to a full sense of its absurdity and wickedness, as to a growing consciousness that the lewd libidinous stare, directed against the jewels of the crown, would in time be transferred to wealth of a more substantial kind, and that the fund-holder and land-owner would come in for a share of that clamour which had hitherto been confined to the pensionist and the reversionist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de97fa0a-1616-4173-8ed0-b191195d0981",
                                "sense_id": "ec17fd19-6a04-332c-873b-dee51e5ed707",
                                "text": "Between the \"occupier\" pure and simple and the freehold reversionist, there are, usually, a large number of intermediate beneficial interests in the property : of which the occupier is probably possessed of a portion and the reversionist of another portion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68bb32be-c160-493f-84c5-f2ca4df859a1",
                                "sense_id": "ec17fd19-6a04-332c-873b-dee51e5ed707",
                                "text": "On the other hand, if land values were subjected to a special rate (as under the terms of Montagu's bill), it would be the occupying and ultimate owner who would suffer - not the intermediate reversionist."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
